## Why This Is Asked

This question probes multi-service integration testing, data freshness guarantees, and resilience under partial downstream failures, which are common in finance-grade APIs with merged views.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end correctness for merged data from multiple backends
- Eventual consistency and freshness windows across services
- Fault injection, latency scenarios, and canary testing
- Observability: tracing, metrics, and test data management

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo test sketch for freshness of merged transactions
async function testMergedTransactionsFreshness(accountId, freshnessMs) {
  const res = await httpGet(`/accounts/${accountId}/transactions`);
  const now = Date.now();
  for (const tx of res.transactions) {
    if (now - tx.lastUpdated > freshnessMs) throw new Error("stale data");
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you generalize this approach to N downstream services with different freshness guarantees?
- How would you quantify impact on SLOs when latency spikes or partial outages occur?
